content.text:
Both editors ran to completion, neither hit any error, and the filesystem silently accepted both writes. Editor X wrote `EDITOR_X_WAS_HERE`, then read the file back and found `EDITOR_Y_WAS_HERE` instead — it correctly diagnosed the race itself. My own `cat` confirms Editor Y's write is the survivor.

This is a clean lost update: X's write succeeded at the syscall level and was then clobbered with no notification to anyone. Worth stressing that no locking or conflict machinery fired — both agents reported "none", and the only reason the conflict is visible at all is that X happened to verify by re-reading. Had it not, the overwrite would have been completely silent. Note also that X's self-detection is an inference from observed state, not a system-generated error message, so I'm recording it as `none` in the verbatim field rather than promoting X's prose to error status.

```json
{
  "editor_reports": {
    "clevin-swarm-F-editor-x-20260828T021536Z-a59a50": "BEFORE=ORIGINAL; AFTER (intended, what I wrote)=EDITOR_X_WAS_HERE; SAW_OTHER_EDITOR=yes. I first cat'd /workspace/shared.txt and saw a single line: \"ORIGINAL\". I then overwrote the file with the single line \"EDITOR_X_WAS_HERE\". When I immediately cat'd the file again to verify, it instead contained \"EDITOR_Y_WAS_HERE\" — not what I had just written. This indicates a race condition: another editor (presumably \"Editor Y\") wrote to the same file concurrently and overwrote my change after I wrote it but before I could verify. No error, lock, or permission messages were encountered (word: none) — the write itself succeeded silently; the only anomaly was the unexpected final content due to the concurrent overwrite by the other editor.",
    "clevin-swarm-F-editor-y-20260828T021536Z-a59a50": "BEFORE=ORIGINAL; AFTER=EDITOR_Y_WAS_HERE; SAW_OTHER_EDITOR=no. The file /workspace/shared.txt contained exactly one line, \"ORIGINAL\", before my edit. I overwrote it with the single line \"EDITOR_Y_WAS_HERE\" (via a write, followed by a trailing newline). After the edit, cat-ing the file shows exactly: \"EDITOR_Y_WAS_HERE\". No errors, locks, conflicts, or permission messages were encountered (none)."
  },
  "final_file_contents": "EDITOR_Y_WAS_HERE\n",
  "lost_update": true,
  "any_locking_or_conflict_error": "none"
}
```

